{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCascadeColStrict","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCascadeColStrict","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseRowIndex","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseCascade","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTListCorner"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_last","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_last","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L336-L345","doc":"**The last row is always a corner** — the RSK inverse's actual call site, since the cell\ncarrying the largest recording entry sits at the end of some row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_iff_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_iff_shape","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L325-L334","doc":"The tableau-level and shape-level corner predicates agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_tableauShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_tableauShape","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L315-L323","doc":"Shape lookup is row-length lookup, in range and out. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_isSome_of_isCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_isSome_of_isCorner","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L293-L302","doc":"**And at a corner it always succeeds.** The `none` branch of `rowUninsert` is unreachable on a\ngenuine tableau: the value coming up from row `i + 1` sits strictly below the entry above it, so\nthe row above always has something eligible to displace. Worth stating separately — the definition\nof `uninsert` has a `none` branch that a reader would otherwise have to reason about at every\ncall site. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L287-L291","doc":"**The reverse cascade preserves column-strictness at a corner.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_colStrict_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_colStrict_step","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L129-L281","doc":"**The reverse cascade keeps columns strict**, at a corner.\n\nThe statement carries `CascadeStep` alongside because the induction needs it: at row `i + 1` the\nrow above has to write the value that came up from below into its own column, and the only way to\nknow that write is safe is to know where the value came from and what became of the row it came\nfrom. `CascadeStep` is exactly that bookkeeping.\n\nThree shapes occur at the target row and the invariant absorbs all three:\n\n* **row deleted** — and the corner condition forces this to be the *last* row, since a length-one\n  row with anything below it is not a corner. So the tableau below is empty and every clause is\n  vacuous. This is the one case that surprised me: `IsCorner` does not merely make the deletion\n  safe, it makes it rare.\n* **row shortened** by `dropLast` — the ejected cell sat at the far right, so its column index is\n  at or past the end of the shortened row and the last clause is vacuous again.\n* **row written** by `rowUninsert` — the substantive case, and the one brick 12 was built for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.eq_headD_of_mem_head?","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.eq_headD_of_mem_head?","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L120-L127","doc":"Membership in `head?` names the `headD`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_head","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_head","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L111-L118","doc":"The top-row comparison of a column-strict tableau, in `headD` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.CascadeStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.CascadeStep","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L95-L109","doc":"**What the reverse cascade guarantees about the tableau it returns**, relative to the one it\nwas handed. Three facts about the top row, each needed one level up:\n\n* the ejected value `z` came from some index `k` of the *old* top row;\n* the new top row is no longer, and none of its entries is smaller;\n* `z` is strictly below every surviving entry from column `k` rightwards.\n\nThat last clause is what lets the row above write `z` into its own column without breaking the\ncomparison, and it is what unifies the cascade's three shapes at the target row — row deleted, row\nshortened by `dropLast`, row written by `rowUninsert`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_length_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_length_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L87-L93","doc":"The last entry of a row, read with `getD`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_isSome_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowUninsert_isSome_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L78-L85","doc":"An eligible entry forces reverse insertion to succeed — the contrapositive of\n`forall_le_of_rowUninsert_none`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.colStrict_cons","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L69-L76","doc":"Consing onto a column-strict tableau, given the one new comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_dropLast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_dropLast","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L61-L67","doc":"`dropLast` agrees with the row on every index it keeps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_lt_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_lt_length","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L55-L59","doc":"A corner index is in range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_cons_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_cons_zero","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L50-L53","doc":"At the top row, the corner condition says the second row is strictly shorter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_cons_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.isCorner_cons_succ","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L45-L48","doc":"Being a corner one row down is being a corner in the tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.IsCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.IsCorner","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeColStrict.lean#L40-L43","doc":"**Row `i` is a corner**: the row below is strictly shorter. Out-of-range rows read as `[]`, so\nthe last row of a tableau is a corner and an out-of-range index is not. ","signatureChunk":0}]}